You see a man with a business suit walk up to your front door. He sees you, however, and approaches you.
The salesman approaches you. "Hello, madam. I am going door to door selling the best product in the world. I tell you this is a product you can't live without. This product will allow you to finally accomplish all those dreams you have of travelling. Yes, no longer will travelling be a problem with the new, waterproof, extra warm in the winter, extra cold in the summer, convenient, ergonomic Super Snuggy!" He produces from his briefcase some kind of orange cloak.

"Now, you might be asking yourself 'What makes this so special?' Well I'm here to tell you that this snuggy was hand woven from Tibetan monks of, well, Tibet, and enchanted by advertising officials in Montana, our headquarters! This snuggy is so warm, Eskimos would be willing to trade a gallon of whale blubber for it! Unfortunately, the Super Snuggy is not available in Alaska, but it is available here, and now you can have it for the low, low price of only $691.05, including sales tax! What do you say?" He looks you over.

>x salesman
He is a confidant man, wearing a gray business suit and carrying a leather briefcase. His black hair is slicked back, and he has a moustache that makes him seem more than a little creepy. When he smiles, you notice that one of his teeth has a gold cap on it. 

>buy snuggy
The salesman looks at the jar of pennies. "Hmm, it's not often we accept this many pennies..." He holds it in his hand for a moment, as if weighing it. "Well, it checks out by weight. Here you go! Enjoy your purchase!" He hands you the snuggy and walks off, happy to have made another sale. You think you hear him mutter "Sucker" after he goes away.

