Computer Room
This room has a history of mis-use. When you first got the house there was a roommate living in this room. When he moved out it was going to be a room for Jeeba's litter box, as so the room stank, and was seldom used. Then the guinea pigs were moved upstairs and the door had to be kept closed to keep the cat out, leaving the room barely used again. Later, when Danny was born, his room had to hold a crib, so a bed got moved in there, making this more of a guest room than a computer room. Many attempts to turn this room into something usable have seen various degrees of success. Once that guinea pig dies, perhaps you'll try again. A large bed takes up a good part of the room, and there are two desks: one which hold an embroidery machine, and one which holds the guinea pig cage. A closet of junk lies in the south wall.

