>consult Wikipedia about spells
Magic is considered to still be at large in the world today. Magic spells can only be cast if you carry a spellbook with the spells inside. It is said that one can reverse the spells by saying the magic words somewhat differently. The wizard of Frobozz once catalogued 69,105 different spells, all beginning with the letter "F". For reference, the correct format for copying spells is to have a spellbook handy, and say "COPY (a scroll)."

>copy fabric scroll
You copy the spell into the spellbook, and watch the fabric scroll disappear!

