The troll's eyes light up. "Ooh! Pot! Gimme Gimme Gimme!" The troll grabs the bag of weed from you. She starts searching her pocket and realizes she has nothing to light the joints with. She looks back at you. "Hey! You got a light?"

>give lighter to troll
(first taking the lighter)
"Fuck yeah!" she says, grabbing the lighter. She lights up a joint. Soon her eyes glaze over. She looks at you. "You're not such a bitch after all, are you?" she says. "Ah, hell, go on ahead!"

>drop pencil box
Dropped.

>w

Grazing Lands
This is a large, beautiful meadow, full of wildflowers. You almost expect to see Julie Andrews running down the field singing "The Hills are Alive", or at the very least the girl from Little House on the Prarie. All around you get to see the beauty of nature, the bright sky, the warm, comfortable air of spring surrounding you, not too hot, not too cold. The grass is tall here, though patches are shorter, as if animals choose this spot to graze. The path ends here. A little ways off the path, you can see what appears to be a rabbit hole.

You can see a billy goat gruff here.

>x goat
He's the clever one that got past the troll earlier. And he does appear a bit gruff, as gruff as a goat can look, I suppose. He has horns, and a goatee. I wonder if that's where they get the term "goatee" from anyway. Well, what do you want from me? He's a goat.

>x hole
In the rabbit hole is a dirty scroll.

>take dirty scroll
Taken.

>read it
Digest: (Turn a horse into poop)
>copy it
You copy the spell into the spellbook, and watch the dirty scroll disappear!

[Your score has just gone up by five points.]

>e

Troll Bridge
The forest clears out a bit here, and opens to a wide plain. Looking around, you can't help but wonder what the united states used to look like before those amber waves of grain were replaced with charcoal waves of concrete. Far to the north it looks like there might be a cabin, you can't get there from here, better to go back through the forest path to your east. A winding river cuts through the plains here, and the path you are on leads over that river to the west, via a stone bridge. 

You can see a pencil box and an an ugly, and very stoned troll here.

>e

Forest Path
You have entered a crossroads in the middle of a forest. The paths go in various directions, from the northwest to the southeast, from the north to the south and southwest, from the west to the east. A large wooden sign seems to provide some direction, and a large beanstalk leads up into the clouds. It looks like it has handhelds and could be climbed. Something about the area here seems fantastic, almost cartoonish. The colors are very bright, and the sky almost looks painted on.

You can see a swirling tunnel of light and magic here.

>sw

Bottom of Hill
You are at the bottom of a very steep hill. Up at the top it looks like there may be a well. The forest clears out a bit here, but continues in all directions around you, becoming quite impenetrable, except by following the path back to the northeast.

You can see Jack and Jill here.

>x Jack
Jack is a man in his late twenties, a country bumpkin by the look of him. His hair is a bit too long, brown, and his face is slightly unshaven, except his goatee, which seems trimmed properly. He is lanky, and of average height. He is kind of attractive, in a scrawny farmer type way. He wears blue jean overalls over a red t-shirt. The top of his head shows sign of hat hair. He seems to favor one of his legs, as if the other one is hurt.

"Keep dreaming, he's my man!" says Jill.

>x Jill
Jill is a girl in her late twenties. She's pretty, and from the look of it, she knows it. She wears a german fraulein girl outfit, specially cut so to be especially sexy (and more than a bit slutty). She wears just a tad too much makeup, and her blond hair has a hint of brown at the roots. She has a look of boredom and annoyance on her face at all times.

"Stop looking at me. Are you some kind of dyke or something?" says Jill.

>ask Jack about Jill
Jack looks over at Jill. "She's the best thing that ever happened to me." he says, though with a hint of nervousness. It almost sounds prepared.

>ask Jack about hill
"Me and Jill went up that hill earlier to, um, to fetch a pail of water. Yeah, that's it. Anyway, we fell down the hill, but my crown is up there, and I want to get it back." he says.

>ask Jack about crown
"My crown is magical, it protects the wearer against all hostile magical spells." says Jack.

>ask Jack about leg
"I hurt my leg falling down the hill and can't get back up." says Jack
>ask Jill about Jack
"My boyfriend is so stupid. He's so lucky to have someone as hot as me!" says Jill.

>ask Jill about hill
"My stupid boyfriend left his magic crown up there. God, he's so stupid!" she says.

>ask Jill about crown
"It's his magic crown. He took it off when we went up there to have sex, and now it's stuck up there!" she tells you.

>u
You try to climb up the hill, but it is too steep to climb up safely. You decide to stop before you fall down and break your crown- the crown of your head that is
>consult Wikipedia about climbing hills
Climbing hills is dangerous business. Falling off can easily mean death. Skilled mountaneers use a variety of equipment, such as crampons, ropes, and pitons to climb mountains and hills. Sorcerers just use magic.

