Building Site
This is a large construction site. It looks like someone started building three houses to start off a subdivision. The forest here has been cleared away, leaving a large clearing, levelled and planted with grass seed. Unfortunately it's not growing yet, so theres thick, rich earth here rather than grass. It is beautifully sunny out.

You can see a stick house, a straw house, a brick house, a stick pig, a straw pig and a brick pig here.

"Looks like she isn't sure where she is." says the brick pig.

>x straw house
A small shack home built out of thatch and mud. On a day like this, it seems like a nice enough home, but you wonder how well such a home would stand up against the elements, or even a strong wind. In fact, you might even be able to punch right through the side of the house.

>x stick house
A bungalow home built primarily out of sticks. As a work of construction, it's pretty impressive, pieces of mud have been placed between the sticks and various nails and ties have been used to make the house waterproof.

>x brick house
This home looks even nicer than your own. Full brick, chimney (implying fireplace), a nice tilted roof with gutters to keep the rain out, and a nice screen porch adorn this two story colonial home. This home looks like a palace compared to the other two homes, and also looks like the only one that will stand the test of time.

