Path of Crumbs
This is a darker part of the forest, where it could be easier to get lost. The path you were on seems to stop around here, and you can hear the sounds of living creatures all around you. The trees have a wicked look about them, some seem to be almost grabbing at you. Though there is thin light piercing through the trees, the area is still full of shadows. Luckily, it's enough light to keep the grues away, in any case. A trail of bread crumbs leads further north, though for how long, it's hard to say, since a number of birds occasionally swoop down and grab a crumb before bringing it back up into the trees. At this point, the path to the south is still visible, though when the sun goes down you could easily become lost here.

The birds seem interested in the jewelled egg.

