From over the distance, it looks like a hungry timber wolf is coming into view. It looks like it has spotted the cows, and is coming to eat. It starts slinking forward, using the stone wall as cover.

>give fish to wolf
(the hungry wolf)
The wolf looks at the fish. It seems entranced by the smell. Instead of going for the cow, it gobbles up the fish instead. However, that didn't seem to fill it up, and it continues to come after the cows. It takes a few steps forward, and starts to hack and choke. You and the boy watch as the wolf starts to vomit, howling and barking madly for a few moments, then collapsing to the ground, apparantly dead. I guess that's what happens- you did poison the fish, after all.

"Oh my god! Thanks a lot!" says the boy. "You've saved my cows. I'm surprised no one else came. But I guess that's what I get for lying so many times. Here, all I can offer you is one of the cows. If you hadn't killed the wolf, he would have taken one anyway, and come back for more. Thanks." He pulls one of the cows from the meadow and leads it over to you.

