You are in the living room of the tiny white house. Toys are scattered all over the room, leaving the floor barely visible. This may be a good thing, because the carpet has numerous stains from recent (and not so recent) pet and baby traffic. The front door leads out to the west, and to the northeast there appears to be a hallway. On the southeast end of the room is a large L shaped couch, which takes up almost all of the south and west walls. A large entertainment center takes up most of the north wall, with half of it being a trophy case, and the other half holding a TV. A baby's high chair is set up in front of the couch, as if there was a recent attempt to feed a child. Stains on the couch and floor indicate that this was most likely an unsuccessful attempt. A large picture window in the west wall gives a view of the street. A closet occupies the northwest corner of the room.  The closet contains a vacuum cleaner.

You can see Luna, Ravi, a crystal ball, a hammer, a remote control, a leaflet, a swirling tunnel of light and magic, a lantern and a sword here.

>ne

The Hallway
This is the nerve center of the entire house, for two reasons. First of all, the thermostat is here, on the south wall, which controls the temperature of the house. Being the only item that controls anything in the house, that makes this officially the control room. Secondly, you can't get from one part of the house to another without going through this room. The hallway is extremely small. A doorway to the southwest leads back to the living room. Another to the west goes to the computer room. The north door goes up some stairs to the master bedroom. To the east is a bathroom. To the southeast is Danny's room, and to the northeast is the Kitchen.

Ravi enters, enticed by your food.

Luna enters, since you have food.

>e

Bathroom
This is the place where you poop. There is a toilet here also. The room is very cramped and hard to move around in. There is a closet here, though it's pretty impossible to open the closet door without first closing the bathroom door. Luckily, we're ignoring doors in this house, so don't worry about it. Besides, there's nothing in the closet, so we'll pretend that isn't here too. The shower is behind you.

