This is the nerve center of the entire house, for two reasons. First of all, the thermostat is here, on the south wall, which controls the temperature of the house. Being the only item that controls anything in the house, that makes this officially the control room. Secondly, you can't get from one part of the house to another without going through this room. The hallway is extremely small. A doorway to the southwest leads back to the living room. Another to the west goes to the computer room. The north door goes up some stairs to the master bedroom. To the east is a bathroom. To the southeast is Danny's room, and to the northeast is the Kitchen.

You can see Ravi here.

>u

Master Bedroom
This is where the magic happens, so to speak. When you originally moved into the house, this was just a small attic full of junk, complete with coil of rope and nasty knife. Since then, you've remodeled the room (this being the only room in the house not still in the condition it was when you move in). Your bed lies against the east wall, and a dresser in the sw corner. A large closet stands next to the door which leads back down to the hallway. There used to be a door to it, but shoddy construction left you throwing the door away. Inside the closet is a footlocker.

You can see a dresser here.

>in

Hidden Crawlspace
This is a small attic area, what's left from before you remodeled the upstairs. There are nails sticking out of the ceiling, and stray insulation everywhere. Other than that, this is a pretty small room without much going on.

You can see a swirling tunnel of light and magic here.

>enter tunnel
Cave
You are in a large underground cave. The place is huge, though it does not seem like there are any exits, apart from a large hole in the ceiling, which goes up out of view (and must twist around, since no light comes from the top). Fear not, for light does come from several torches around the cave, and glitters from the giant mound of treasure you see before you. Gold, silver, jewels, diamonds, all sorts of treasure is here.  The most notable treasure is a large golden box with the insignia of a heart on it.

You can see a swirling tunnel of light and magic here.

>open golden box
You open the golden box, revealing a giant heart.

>x heart
It is a heart, just like a human heart, but rather than being the size of your fist, it's about double the size of your head. It pulsates, still beating, despite not being in a body.

>take it
Taken.

