Path of Crumbs
This is a darker part of the forest, where it could be easier to get lost. The path you were on seems to stop around here, and you can hear the sounds of living creatures all around you. The trees have a wicked look about them, some seem to be almost grabbing at you. Though there is thin light piercing through the trees, the area is still full of shadows. Luckily, it's enough light to keep the grues away, in any case. A trail of bread crumbs leads further north, though for how long, it's hard to say, since a number of birds occasionally swoop down and grab a crumb before bringing it back up into the trees. At this point, the path to the south is still visible, though when the sun goes down you could easily become lost here.

You can see a jewelled egg here.

>n

Outside Gingerbread House
You have wandered up to a house in the dark woods. It's made out of what appears to be bread and candy! It almost looks like you walked up to a giant cake with a door! The windows appear to be some form or rock candy- letting through what little light there is here, while not letting you quite see inside. Puffs of smoke resembling cotton candy come from the chimney, the door seems to be some kind of graham cracker with a chocolate handle. You can't help but wonder how a house can be made out of perishables, but I guess there's a giant beanstalk leading up into the clouds a bit to the south, so this must just be a weird place.  From inside you can hear what sounds like a hag cackling.

>eat house
(first taking the piece of gingerbread house)
You break off a piece. It's actually pretty good. You also watch in amazement as the piece you broke off seems to grow back and replenish the house, until you can't even see the part you removed. Ah, magic. Of course.

>n

Inside Gingerbread House
This place, which looked so cheery and fresh on the outside, looks more like a dungeon on the inside. There is a small, furnished bedroom, probably where the master of the house sleeps, and an assortment of small cells on the opposite walls, all empty. A large stove is set in the north wall, baking something that smells like meat pies.

There is an arcane book here on a shelf.

You can also see a witch and a potion box here.

